// rim it is not: a tumbleweed does not climb down a cliff, it is blown
// off it. So the road leaves the rim level and falls in an arc through
// the air to the ledge, crosses what there is of its top, goes off the
// lip in a second, shorter arc to the foot of the skirt, and is the
// land surface again from there. It runs on a little past both edges of
// the box so the weed arrives from off the page and leaves the same
